sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task (driver workflow), Recall deps-one-group-per-project + deps-update-test-agent-on-failure, R1-R2.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: project:maintenance:routine
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  CLI->>GW: maintenance:routine 4<br/>--idempotency-key=KEY
  %%> Command:
  %%> - MCP tool `project-maintenance-routine` with project `4` and an Idempotency-Key
  %%> - syntax: `project:maintenance:routine <project> --idempotency-key=KEY`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Project ID
  %%> - an idempotency key; it is required, so a lost reply replays the same task
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the MCP tool; there is no `orbit` CLI page for it yet
  %%> - the hourly `maintenance-projects` Schedule admits the same kind when a Project's weekly routine is due
  Note over GW: Validate, capture state<br/>task #5151 · no token
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Gateway
  %%> - Project 4 reads its repository through the GitHub App
  %%> - Project 4 has a default branch and a task check
  %%> - no other `project.detect`, `project.routine` or `project.observe` task runs for Project 4
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - captures the Project, its task groups and the admission time
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - no GitHub token: routine selection reads nothing outside the captured state
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5151 recorded, kind `project.routine`, driver `workflow`, on Node 209
  %%> - no Node is a target
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>project-routine
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the captured Project, task groups and admission time
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5151
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the caller follows the task with `operation:show`
  Note over SW: Read the admitted input<br/>project-maintenance-input read
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks that the input names Project 4 and Node 209
  Note over SW: Select this week's routine<br/>orbit-gateway schedule_project
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - builds the routine key for Project 4 and this week
  %%> - compares it with the routine records Swamp keeps
  %%> Blocked when:
  %%> - Project 4 has another unfinished task group or a task group with a workspace
  %%> - an earlier attempt with this key has no known result
  %%> Result:
  %%> - one routine group request, or none with the blocking reason
  %%> Why no admission here:
  %%> - steps never call the Gateway; the request travels in the terminal result
  alt selection done
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · requests
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Admit the routine group<br/>task group #813 · tasks.provision
    %%> Result with a request:
    %%> - task group #813 created for the routine, or the existing one with the same brief reused
    %%> - the Gateway admits `tasks.provision`; the routine's updates run in its task VM, and a Pi turn starts only when tests fail
    %%> Result without a request:
    %%> - no task group; the blocking reason is in the result
    %%> Always:
    %%> - task #5151 succeeds
  else input or selection fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> When:
    %%> - the input is invalid or Swamp's routine records can't be read
    Note over GW: Mark the task failed<br/>no group · rerun is safe
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5151 fails; no task group is created
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the command again with a new key, or wait for the next hourly Schedule fire
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5151
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the admitted group IDs once the task has ended
  end
